The _shrink API can cause upgrades, conﬁguration changes, and domain deletions to fail. We
don't recommend using it on domains that run Elasticsearch versions 5.3 or 5.1. These versions
have a bug that can cause snapshot restoration of shrunken indices to fail.
Notable API diﬀerences
1912
Amazon OpenSearch Service
Developer Guide
If you use the _shrink API on other Elasticsearch or OpenSearch versions, make the following
request before starting the shrink operation:
PUT https://domain-name.region.es.amazonaws.com/source-index/_settings
{
"settings": {
"index.routing.allocation.require._name": "name-of-the-node-to-shrink-to",
"index.blocks.read_only": true
}
}
Then make the following requests after completing the shrink operation:
PUT https://domain-name.region.es.amazonaws.com/source-index/_settings
{
"settings": {
"index.routing.allocation.require._name": null,
"index.blocks.read_only": false
}
}
PUT https://domain-name.region.es.amazonaws.com/shrunken-index/_settings
{
"settings": {
"index.routing.allocation.require._name": null,
"index.blocks.read_only": false
}
}
